<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn al-Muqarrab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn al-Muqarrab al-Uyuni was an Arabic poet from al-Ahsa in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and a member of the Uyunid ruling family. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwan</a>, praising and lamenting members of the dynasty and complaining of his own treatment, was later furnished with a long commentary. Poem and commentary together are the main source for the history of the Uyunid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>.</p></div>
